# LLP 0013 Hermes patch 0007 — fail closed on the async/deputy attribution boundary
# Class: B (a header sentinel constant + one-line changes to two existing functions).
# @ref LLP 0013#mechanism-3, Open-Q3 (native/microtask attribution)
#
# Closes a deputy-laundering hole in enforce mode: a package could exfiltrate a
# host capability by DETACHING a deputy method from its own frame — passing it
# directly as a promise/timer callback (`Promise.resolve(x).then(fs.readFileSync)`)
# so the reaction runs with no package frame on the stack. Two fixes:
#
#   * getCurrentPackageId returned 0 (the first-party root principal) BOTH for a
#     genuine first-party frame AND when the walk found no user frame at all.
#     With the host trusting root 0 (so `--capsec enforce` is usable), the
#     no-user-frame case fell open. Now it returns a distinct kNoUserPrincipal
#     (0xFFFFFFFE, declared in CapabilityAttribution.h so eval-site callers can
#     exclude it too) that the host fails closed on — genuine first-party (a
#     frame stamped 0) still returns 0 and stays trusted.
#
#   * The internal bytecode (Hermes's JS Promise implementation) loaded during
#     Runtime construction with the default principal 0, so its reaction
#     trampoline (`tryCallOne`) sat on the stack of every microtask job labelled
#     packageId 0 — indistinguishable from first-party root. It is a runtime
#     deputy: stamp its Domain with the runtime principal (0xFFFFFFFF) so the
#     frame walk skips it and reaches kNoUserPrincipal for a detached deputy.
#
# Together: the app's own async work (its callback carries principal 0) is still
# trusted; a dependency's detached-deputy op reaches no user frame and is denied.
# Red-team: tests/llp0013_compartments.rs
# detached_deputy_read_is_contained_but_app_wrapped_read_works.
#
diff --git a/include/hermes/VM/CapabilityAttribution.h b/include/hermes/VM/CapabilityAttribution.h
index e571e81..b583c2a 100644
--- a/include/hermes/VM/CapabilityAttribution.h
+++ b/include/hermes/VM/CapabilityAttribution.h
@@ -27,9 +27,22 @@ namespace vm {
 class Runtime;
 class JSObject;
 
-/// \return the capability principal (package id) of the nearest JS frame on the
-/// stack, or 0 (trusted root / unassigned) when no attributable JS frame is
-/// found. Skips native frames, whose callee CodeBlock is null.
+/// The principal getCurrentPackageId() returns when the stack has NO
+/// attributable user frame (only native and/or runtime-deputy frames) — e.g. a
+/// deputy method passed directly as a promise/timer callback
+/// (`Promise.resolve(x).then(fs.readFileSync)`). DISTINCT from the first-party
+/// root principal 0 (which the host trusts) and from the runtime principal
+/// 0xFFFFFFFF: the host fails closed on this sentinel, and a caller that pins a
+/// captured principal onto a Domain must exclude it (it is not a real package id
+/// and is not transparent to the frame walk). @ref LLP 0013 Open-Q3
+/// (native/microtask attribution).
+constexpr uint32_t kNoUserPrincipal = 0xFFFFFFFEu;
+
+/// \return the capability principal of the nearest user JS frame on the stack:
+/// 0 (trusted first-party root) for a genuine root frame, a package id for a
+/// package frame, or kNoUserPrincipal when no user frame is attributable. Skips
+/// native frames (null callee CodeBlock) and runtime-deputy frames (principal
+/// 0xFFFFFFFF).
 uint32_t getCurrentPackageId(Runtime &runtime);
 
